> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/genealogy-salubri.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/genealogy-salubri.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/family-tree-salubri.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/family-tree-salubri.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/family-tree-salubri.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/10/family-tree-salubri.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I ask the source of Elyon, childe of Adonai? I only ask as I can't find a reference for it anywhere, and I play a Salubri antitribu grandchilde of Adonai named Elyon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/699-malleusxxiii","name":"MalleusXXIII","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar699_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T10:56:25-08:00","id":1555063,"title":"","content":"Scatha-Columbkille is Baradiel's kid but I don't really remember Baradiel is the Child of Gabriel<br /> Nor Simon ben-Yaakov is the Child of Nahum ben Enosh<br /> Tho' there is a 4th gen Yakov from TC2,p85....\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T12:32:11-08:00","id":1555066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555053#post1555053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a shame, as their concepts were pretty much all designed by Central and Southern Americans with a good knowledge of regional folklore. What part of them was offensive?</div> </div> </div> </div>With all due respect, the intention itself. There are a 13 clans with previous lore on the whole central and south america and now suddenly it's all gone. The Tlacique were really a good addition as a conflict point, but the drowned legacies.is just unknown clans with yes, carefully researched local lore but that's not what we generally are here. I'm extremely open for an entire Drowned Legacies book in which it explains everything. When and if that comes out, it can probably change my mind.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T12:43:32-08:00","id":1555068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555055#post1555055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont know if you've ever seen it but there was <a href=\"http://vampirerpg.free.fr/Genealogy/\" target=\"_blank\">this old Genealogy list</a> from years ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember this one, its probably the reason I started mine on the first place. It was kinda messy and incomplete (so is mine, still).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T12:56:25-08:00","id":1555070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MalleusXXIII</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555060#post1555060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can I ask the source of Elyon, childe of Adonai? I only ask as I can't find a reference for it anywhere, and I play a Salubri antitribu grandchilde of Adonai named Elyon...</div> </div> </div> </div>Elyon is probably an entry I created for my chronicles. I can't find it anywhere on the genealogies. Justin Achilli might know more about Adonai, he wrote down his stats but never published them (we know this from a comment of his back on the old white-wolf forums).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 11-04-2025, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T13:08:50-08:00","id":1555072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555063#post1555063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scatha-Columbkille is Baradiel's kid but I don't really remember Baradiel is the Child of Gabriel<br /> Nor Simon ben-Yaakov is the Child of Nahum ben Enosh<br /> Tho' there is a 4th gen Yakov from TC2,p85....</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole Scatha, Baradiel and Gabriel on the family tree is just me filling up the dots of the unknown. I probably used it on a chronicle long ago. Remeber that the family trees are most accurate on what is published and the other part is just me, filling up the blanks. I usually use location the Cainite and approximate age of embrace. Since during the Dark Ages Cainites usually didn't travel much, I used those references as guide for whenever I needed to establish a whole lineage for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T16:23:40-08:00","id":1555077,"title":"","content":"While I don't know much about them yet, the Drowned Legacies seem a lot like what they did with KotE and KotEK, even if a better execution.<br /> <br /> The problem isn't so much with how they are, but the fact that the main game wasn't thought with most of the world in mind, and then they &quot;solve&quot; it not by making the main game more versatile and something that could accommodate more people, but by making a different game for those other areas.<br /> <br /> Requiem has clans that are universal, and then makes stuff through limited bloodlines. It works. C20 did regional kiths everywhere, but Changeling has the pass that the Kiths are heavily Irish to begin with, so whatever, and all Changelings are still the same kind of creature.<br /> <br /> VtM did this weird thing where other continents get completely different creatures that may or may not be related to Cainites. It's weird, and not very welcoming.<br /> <br /> And that said: I like KotEK anyway, and I think KotE is a good concept in the wrong place. As I said, I don't know enough of the Drowned Legacies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T18:42:06-08:00","id":1555085,"title":"","content":"Clan Lasombra<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-lasombra.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/family-tree-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/family-tree-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/family-tree-lasombra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/family-tree-lasombra.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-04T22:35:37-08:00","id":1555092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555072#post1555072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole Scatha, Baradiel and Gabriel on the family tree is just me filling up the dots of the unknown. I probably used it on a chronicle long ago. Remeber that the family trees are most accurate on what is published and the other part is just me, filling up the blanks. I usually use location the Cainite and approximate age of embrace. Since during the Dark Ages Cainites usually didn't travel much, I used those references as guide for whenever I needed to establish a whole lineage for my chronicles.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sense<br /> I tend to do the same, for the Tzimisce for example, grasping very loose ceonnections, like with Jedrik<br /> <br /> Jedrik (5th Generation)<br /> Children of (probably) Triglav (sadly no official information, whos Children Jedrik was, but considering Cracow is relatively close to Prague where Shaagra ruled, whos sire was the mighty Koldun-Prophet, Triglav)<br /> Sire of Razkoljna<br /> Koldun. After 930 Jedrik and Razkoljna found themselves under attack by a group of sword-wielding warriors led by priests armed with holy water and other symbols of their faith. The fight was bitter. All of the warriors fell, but not before they struck Jedrik\u2019s head from his body.<br /> [Transylvania by Night]<br /> <br /> Djabelek, Master of Bia\u0142owieza Forest (6th)<br /> Children of probbably Jedrik (Transylvania by Night describes Jedrik the master of Poland, where the Bia\u0142owieza is)<br /> Sire of Sarolt Grondrska<br /> [V20 Dark Ages Tome of Secrets]<br /> <br /> Sarolt Grondrska, the Boar, Koldun of Bia\u0142owieza (7th)<br /> Children Djabelek<br /> [V20 Dark Ages Tome of Secrets]\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-05T00:55:00-08:00","id":1555099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1555068#post1555068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I remember this one, its probably the reason I started mine on the first place. It was kinda messy and incomplete (so is mine, still).<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I mention it, because it would help you cross reference the npcs, since every book they have information is listed.<br /> <br /> Secondly I'd suggest not labeling the Baali as being childer of Saulot because it is never -canonically- confirmed. It is just one of the multiple choice origins for them. IMO Shaitan/Huitzl/Chaos Factor guy, is more likely to be a childe of Cappadocius than Saulot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-07T14:11:01-08:00","id":1555216,"title":"","content":"Malkavian are up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-malkavian.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-malkavian.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-malkavian.html\" target=\"_blank\"> https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/genealogy-malkavian.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2025/11/family-tree-malkavian.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> 