],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T04:06:02-07:00","id":1561341,"title":"","content":"I had to migrate the timeline from the original post due to it being to large to be saved.<br /> <br /> So now its divided in 3 parts:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/07/timeline-of-vampire-masquerade-part-1.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/0...de-part-1.html</a> (before common era)<br /> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/07/timeline-of-vampire-masquerade-part-2.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/0...de-part-2.html</a><a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/07/timeline-of-vampire-masquerade-part-2.html%E2%80%8B\" target=\"_blank\">\u200b</a> (common era - anarch revolt)<br /> <a href=\"https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/07/timeline-of-vampire-masquerade-part-3.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://saga1982.blogspot.com/2026/0...de-part-3.html</a> (convention of thorns - gehenna/20th anniversary)\u200b<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-05-2026, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T11:42:40-07:00","id":1561350,"title":"","content":"I have to admit that to even attempt to cover the various and contradictory history of VTM is impressive and shows more dedication then many fans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T15:23:11-07:00","id":1561354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561350#post1561350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit that to even attempt to cover the various and contradictory history of VTM is impressive and shows more dedication then many fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you all for the feedback, suggestions and the +1900 views!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's hard. I plan to edit the &quot;{WRONG}&quot; entries once i'm done with it all and establish them as &quot;# given date&quot;. It does give a headache with entries like Mithras, Quetzalcoatl and Tezcatlipoca since they are mentioned as being many supernaturals (mage, Cainite / Pooka, mage / Cainite, wraith). Crossover entities are problematic and hard to write a comprehensible entry for them. Still, long way from finishing it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T16:11:14-07:00","id":1561355,"title":"","content":"This is an extremely ambitious and far reaching project and I love that you\u2019re doing it for the people who hang out on the forums.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T14:06:57-07:00","id":1561434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561354#post1561354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you all for the feedback, suggestions and the +1900 views!<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's hard. I plan to edit the &quot;{WRONG}&quot; entries once i'm done with it all and establish them as &quot;# given date&quot;. It does give a headache with entries like Mithras, Quetzalcoatl and Tezcatlipoca since they are mentioned as being many supernaturals (mage, Cainite / Pooka, mage / Cainite, wraith). Crossover entities are problematic and hard to write a comprehensible entry for them. Still, long way from finishing it.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Tezcatlipoca is also a demon in <i>Mage</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T14:21:25-07:00","id":1561436,"title":"","content":"Re: the Treaty of Tyre and Convention of Thorns thing, the sources don't contradict if you assume the elders who signed the Convention in 1493 did not have the authority to bind the clan (this is often argued to be because they were captives, though this varies). The Assamites then ignored the Convention until the Camarilla forced them to sign in 1496 (after a Nosferatu gets into Alamut). When the Amr signed, he effectively had the permission to sign on behalf of all clan loyalists (not the antitribu) and that's why the curse worked. V20 mentions as much in BJD and Lore of the Clans, as well, but it's in the clanbooks, too, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T15:24:38-07:00","id":1561438,"title":"","content":"A couple more comments:<ul><li>Per p. 95 of CbARev, Jamal took the Black Throne in 1497. Izhim and his followers left two weeks after that, putting their exodus firmly in 1497. Elsewhere, the book says he ruled from 1494, but that's obviously a mistake as he diablerises the Amr in 1496 before taking the Black Throne.</li> <li>Caine's Chosen merely says Izhim and Djuhah join the Black Hand after the Treaty of Tyre and before the lost colony at Roanoke was founded (1587). Putting a date span might be more accurate. With what we know about their exodus, 1497\u20131587 makes sense.</li> <li>Also, we technically don't know how soon after they joined the Sabbat that it was before Vestgeir asked them to sever contact with their main clan. You could just soften the word (&quot;Some time after...&quot;, etc.).</li> <li>I can't find a particular date for Fariq's defection, but it's said he didn't go to the Convention of Thorns and was &quot;immediately&quot; branded antitribu by his clanmates (TC3, p. 80). Now, this could mean immediately after the Convention (1493) or, more likely, immediately after the Treaty of Tyre (1496). So 1496 makes a better date for that, but &quot;after 1496&quot; would also work.</li> <li>Re: Karsh/Jalan-Aajav/Qarakh, the last of these is never actually confirmed to be 4th Generation as far as I've been able to confirm. He diablerised a Methuselah but was only 7th Generation at the time (and that's after diablerising his sire). In all likelihood, he would've been 5th or 6th Generation afterwards, not 4th. It's therefore more likely that it's just the same person flitting between the two sects (Jalan-Aajav in particular seems to vanish for large periods of time), or there's another solution. Not really a timeline thing, but worth bearing in mind.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T15:43:21-07:00","id":1561439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561436#post1561436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: the Treaty of Tyre and Convention of Thorns thing, the sources don't contradict if you assume the elders who signed the Convention in 1493 did not have the authority to bind the clan (this is often argued to be because they were captives, though this varies). The Assamites then ignored the Convention until the Camarilla forced them to sign in 1496 (after a Nosferatu gets into Alamut). When the Amr signed, he effectively had the permission to sign on behalf of all clan loyalists (not the antitribu) and that's why the curse worked. V20 mentions as much in BJD and Lore of the Clans, as well, but it's in the clanbooks, too, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the first story of the Convention of Thorns was on TC2 (VtDA which was 2nd ed times, pre Revised) and many of those who assisted were mentioned later on Revised. It was supposed to be all happening there (the Treaty of Tyre IIRC was introduced on Clanbook Assamite 2nd which modified that book from happening as it did (i'm guessing on writing timeline, not publishing timeline). I try to give the most comprehensive view of it all having that in mind. I'll later answer all your comments, thanks for the insight.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T16:32:19-07:00","id":1561440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561434#post1561434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tezcatlipoca is also a demon in <i>Mage</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Cooking pause) Tezcatlipoca was a demon in Mage?! In which book is that explained? Mage is the line 2nd gameline I know the least (1st being Changeling).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T18:44:56-07:00","id":1561442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561438#post1561438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple more comments:<ul><li>Per p. 95 of CbARev, Jamal took the Black Throne in 1497. Izhim and his followers left two weeks after that, putting their exodus firmly in 1497. Elsewhere, the book says he ruled from 1494, but that's obviously a mistake as he diablerises the Amr in 1496 before taking the Black Throne.</li> <li>Caine's Chosen merely says Izhim and Djuhah join the Black Hand after the Treaty of Tyre and before the lost colony at Roanoke was founded (1587). Putting a date span might be more accurate. With what we know about their exodus, 1497\u20131587 makes sense.</li> <li>Also, we technically don't know how soon after they joined the Sabbat that it was before Vestgeir asked them to sever contact with their main clan. You could just soften the word (&quot;Some time after...&quot;, etc.).</li> <li>I can't find a particular date for Fariq's defection, but it's said he didn't go to the Convention of Thorns and was &quot;immediately&quot; branded antitribu by his clanmates (TC3, p. 80). Now, this could mean immediately after the Convention (1493) or, more likely, immediately after the Treaty of Tyre (1496). So 1496 makes a better date for that, but &quot;after 1496&quot; would also work.</li> <li>Re: Karsh/Jalan-Aajav/Qarakh, the last of these is never actually confirmed to be 4th Generation as far as I've been able to confirm. He diablerised a Methuselah but was only 7th Generation at the time (and that's after diablerising his sire). In all likelihood, he would've been 5th or 6th Generation afterwards, not 4th. It's therefore more likely that it's just the same person flitting between the two sects (Jalan-Aajav in particular seems to vanish for large periods of time), or there's another solution. Not really a timeline thing, but worth bearing in mind.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Jamal; He was first mentioned on Clanbook Assamite 2nd, then expanded on Revised meanwhile Dark Ages Revised mentioned Nakurtum became Old Man (Woman) of the Mountain during the Dark Ages after Sha'hiri (Thetmes' sire). I do believe it was Nakurtum who got ritually diablerized after the Treaty of Tyre but I keep that storyline to my own (non-published, though the first draft had a lot of &quot;{me}&quot; entries) timeline.<br /> <br /> Caine's Chosen, and much of Revised era books, storylines are written in 1st person testimonies, that make datelining the story really hard, so I try to stay true to those stories that are shared between all editions. Imagine that a single Conditioning (Dominate 4) would mess up everything I make an entry upon (obviously there's the &quot;someone Dominated and made X vampire express X thing back in 2nd ed&quot; and that would render all my effort pointless&quot;). On the Lost Tribe specifically I carry things from 1st and 2nd ed all the way to Revised since almost before Gehenna we get the comprehensible book about them.<br /> <br /> Fariq: yeah, really not a lot specific on that one, but get used to it, I measure things like that there because I know I'll get moments when embracing dates will become impossible to date. Like Triglav embracing Velya, Djavakhi embracing Noriz (this one I wrote today). Have in mind that 2nd ed had the Second City dated back to 5000 BC (Chaos Factor -&gt; Shaitan) aprox and on '94 archaeological evidence discovered Gobleki Tepe (very few linked to archaeology knew this back then and I doubt white-wolf linked to this), I had my theories back on 2nd ed published materials but that got off track really fast when current archaeology caught up.<br /> <br /> Vestgeir: there's only one sentence of him on PGttS, that's it, nothing more (perhaps there's an VtES entry). I really can't expand more of it without being completely ignored on Revised era.<br /> <br /> Karsh/Jalan: I give this on the old white-wolf forumite perspective. This is a thing we discussed a lot back in the day! I understand that the site closed after 2004 but those were really good times. Qarakh came a lot later than those theories (remember that Guide to the Camarilla haven't been published yet, and we still considered that Protean 9 was still &quot;Dual Form&quot;). When Children of the Night came out we had a lot of discussion about it on the forums. Remember that Qarakh came a lot later in Winds from the East and later even when he diablerized Alexander in Dark Ages Revised (Alexander's concept changed from VtDA to DA: V). Having that into consideration, Karsh got staked and disappeared in Brujah Trilogy Novels (I haven't write those ones yet) and Meonia (an elder/methuselah True Brujah) and his childer, Claudia and Rodrigo kills Xaviar. Jalan Aajav disappeared too when Lucita tries to contact him during Gehenna: Final Night. This storyline might have been amazing if Dark Ages: Italy and Brujah Chronicles got to be published since it explained the True Brujah involvment during the fall of Carthage (but those never came to be pubilshed).<br /> <br /> Remember I try to give as much from 1st ed, 2nd ed, and Revised primarily. I really can't take BJD to replace everything on all previous editions since it actually does that (Anatole dies in '99 after the &quot;Leopold&quot; incident in the clan novels, Theo Bell commits diablerie on a Tal'mahe'Ra Malkavian, Lucita, Giangalieazzo, Hardestadt and Okulos die in '04). Therefore I only take what can be retconned to old stuff.<br /> <br /> Let's do this, give me the sources (book and pages #) and I'll see how can I add it. Have in mind that stuff like Katherine de Monpellier from Cb-TR messes up everything so that might take a while to be redacted.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-07-2026, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T02:54:56-07:00","id":1561454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561440#post1561440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Cooking pause) Tezcatlipoca was a demon in Mage?! In which book is that explained? Mage is the line 2nd gameline I know the least (1st being Changeling).<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Book of Madness 1st Edition Pg. 91","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T03:20:38-07:00","id":1561455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561454#post1561454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Book of Madness 1st Edition Pg. 91</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, but It's the revised edition from 2001.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T03:31:10-07:00","id":1561456,"title":"","content":"I'd say any mythical name employed by a supernatural, especially a god, should be taken as a <i><b>claim </b></i>by default.<br /> <br /> So there's a Vampire that <i>claims</i> the name Tezcatlipoca, and there's a &quot;demon&quot; in Mage that makes a similar claim.<br /> <br /> Any relation between the two and/or the myth of Tezcatlipoca is up in the air.<br /> <br /> That way you can reconcile the fact that, let's be clear, several individuals of any splat can and will claim such names at some point. They should not be ever assumed as the real deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T03:54:13-07:00","id":1561459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561456#post1561456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say any mythical name employed by a supernatural, especially a god, should be taken as a <i><b>claim </b></i>by default.<br /> <br /> So there's a Vampire that <i>claims</i> the name Tezcatlipoca, and there's a &quot;demon&quot; in Mage that makes a similar claim.<br /> <br /> Any relation between the two and/or the myth of Tezcatlipoca is up in the air.<br /> <br /> That way you can reconcile the fact that, let's be clear, several individuals of any splat can and will claim such names at some point. They should not be ever assumed as the real deal.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>*Mutters &quot;Rasputin&quot; and leaves*</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T04:14:33-07:00","id":1561461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561459#post1561459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>*Mutters &quot;Rasputin&quot; and leaves*</i></div> </div> </div> </div>He's not a myth, he's an actual, verified person.<br /> <br /> And in WoD, Sam Haight probably dreamed to become Rasputin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T05:53:15-07:00","id":1561465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561456#post1561456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say any mythical name employed by a supernatural, especially a god, should be taken as a <i><b>claim </b></i>by default.<br /> <br /> So there's a Vampire that <i>claims</i> the name Tezcatlipoca, and there's a &quot;demon&quot; in Mage that makes a similar claim.<br /> <br /> Any relation between the two and/or the myth of Tezcatlipoca is up in the air.<br /> <br /> That way you can reconcile the fact that, let's be clear, several individuals of any splat can and will claim such names at some point. They should not be ever assumed as the real deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which type of mythology we're dealing with.<br /> <br /> Not all ancient faiths believed their gods lived in some extradimensional plane of existence.<br /> <br /> The ancient Greeks, for example, believed their gods lived on earth, and you could theoretically visit them if you were able to climb to the peak of Mount Olympus.<br /> <br /> So, if an ancient Koldun came down from the mountains, and demonstrated the power to throw lightning bolts, while claiming to be Zeus, then who are we to challenge it?<br /> <br /> Vampires have walked the earth for nearly as long as humanity itself. Statistically speaking, at least a few of those vampires had to be the origin for a few pantheons, instead of impersonating them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 07-08-2026, 08:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T08:28:48-07:00","id":1561469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561461#post1561461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He's not a myth, he's an actual, verified person.<br /> <br /> And in WoD, Sam Haight probably dreamed to become Rasputin.</div> </div> </div> </div>In our world he was an actual person, I don't know what that has to do with the game tho.<br /> <br /> In WoD he has been couple(?) of vampires of different clans, a Shadow Lord garou, a Cult of Ecstasy mage... and/or Puppeteer Wraith who pretended to be all of those. <br /> <br /> The bottom line with Rasputin and all the other historical/mythical/religious figures as supernaturals in World of Darkness is their true nature is up for debate. Was Rasputin a mortal that was turned into a vampire or did one of the Cainites stole his identity for his own purposes? Or maybe he was a garou or mage in service to the Romanoffs. Was he possessed by a Wraith after he was executed or was he possessed long before that? Or was all of that a prank done by one of the Changelings? The books provide contradictory answers for those questions. <br /> <br /> Of course in reality writers take names that sound cool unaware or ignoring the fact that those names have already been used. And then people argue whether Mithras was a god whose name was taken by a Ventrue Methuselah or was the Ventrue Methuselah responsible for formation of mithraic cults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:07:21-07:00","id":1561486,"title":"","content":"Third time lucky with the spam filter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561439#post1561439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, the first story of the Convention of Thorns was on TC2 (VtDA which was 2nd ed times, pre Revised) and many of those who assisted were mentioned later on Revised. It was supposed to be all happening there (the Treaty of Tyre IIRC was introduced on Clanbook Assamite 2nd which modified that book from happening as it did (i'm guessing on writing timeline, not publishing timeline). I try to give the most comprehensive view of it all having that in mind. I'll later answer all your comments, thanks for the insight.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem. The timeline is definitely a mess and the <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i> are also riddled with date errors, even between the books in the series itself. Some plot elements also just get plain retconned in later books. For example, TC4 also says that Tremere himself had to wake up and curse both the Assamites and the Tremere <i>antitribu</i>, with the implication being that he did both at the same time or close together. But elsewhere the <i>antitribu</i> get cursed after the clan compiles the names of the suspected defectors, and the date given for the latter is different again. Similarly, TC4 says Goratrix is probably dead, and Tremere left his soul to pass on or whatever, but didn't care about protecting it. Yet <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> says Tremere keeps his soul safe in a crystal mirror, until the time he finds a suitable replacement body.<br /> <br /> <i>Clanbook: Assamite</i> came out in 1995, while TC2 was 1998, so I think the authors of TC2 just didn't read it or went with something different because they wanted to tell a particular story. But ultimately, I figure that the Treaty of Tyre wouldn't have been necessary at all if the Assamites had already been successfully cursed, so I treat it as the Convention not being enough to curse the whole clan.<br /> <br /> As another factor, the Baali Curse didn't work all that well initially, either. They had to capture Izhim abd'Azrael (and 11 others) and give him to Namtaru for it to finally spread effectively.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561440#post1561440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Cooking pause) Tezcatlipoca was a demon in Mage?! In which book is that explained? Mage is the line 2nd gameline I know the least (1st being Changeling).<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised did this thing where they implied certain powerful elders might have been demons or spirits all along. Tezcatlipoca is implied to be either a vampire or spirit in VTM, but the same goes for Huitzilopochtli. Interestingly, the MTAs section on Tezcatlipoca says that Huitzilopochtli is one of his avatars, implying they're both the same being. That means Nergal maybe got retconned out of VTM for a hot second.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T18:58:53-07:00","id":1561496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561465#post1561465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on which type of mythology we're dealing with.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, I wasn't talking about characters believing, I was talking about how we as readers should read the lore.<br /> <br /> First instinct is to read that if a given individual is named Odin in the setting, then he's in the setting the original Odin.<br /> <br /> But this is a wrong assumption.<br /> <br /> Actually there exists a myth of Odin, people that posed as the mythical Odin, spirits that act as Odin, and other, stranger possibilities, like an actual Godhead Odin.<br /> <br /> Without undeniable proof, which we'll never get, there's no way to say which came first and who's based on who. Any of them can be the original, any of them can be the origin of a given tale or aspect of the myth, and any of them can still have cults and/or answer prayers and rituals. Including the myth itself, the story.<br /> <br /> So, for us, readers, the claim is just a claim. It can't be verified outside one's own table.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561469#post1561469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In our world he was an actual person, I don't know what that has to do with the game tho.<br /> <br /> The bottom line with Rasputin and all the other historical/mythical/religious figures as supernaturals in World of Darkness is their true nature is up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking nature, I'm talking identity.<br /> <br /> We know who Rasputin were in the setting. We don't know what he was, we don't know what he is today, we don't know a lot of things about him.<br /> <br /> But the basic gist of this plebeian monk who had access to the Tsarina, walked Sankt-Peterburg as if he owned the place and died in a way that scared his assassins, we know the figure and his famous shenanigans as facts.<br /> <br /> Not so much for old gods. We don't know the original facts about any of them. We don't know what the first entity being identified as one of them looks like. We don't know any fact that can be used to say &quot;this identity surely belonged to this entity at this time, this was the real one everyone's talking about&quot;.<br /> <br /> And it has nothing to do with the writers being careless. It's about the consistency we intuitively expect being actually bullshit.<br /> <br /> The writers aren't just taking cool names. They wove the original legend in, not making the character a faithful fit, but making a plausible candidate.<br /> <br /> On top of that, seriously: no one has to be &quot;the real thing&quot; to claim it. Even to think they are it. We have plenty of people through history that claimed to be Jesus either returned or immortal, in fact we still have some quite famous. I know about two at least. Those people believe what they say.<br /> <br /> That's how the world actually works. So what wouldn't actually make sense would be for any of those myths to have a fixed, undeniable origin and original identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T00:15:41-07:00","id":1561505,"title":"","content":"It's also a well established thing that vampires are liars and set themselves up as blood gods wherever they go. So I tend to agree that any vampire labelled &quot;God X&quot; is just that\u2014a vampire behind a fa\u00e7ade, rather than the origin of the God X myth.<br /> <br /> There are probably some exceptions (sometimes the book says, OOC, that so-and-so was the real inspiration for the myth of God Y), but those are rare and maybe even then are unreliable or simply indicating a vampire who made the myth of God Y <i>more famous</i>, rather than inventing it altogether.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T05:19:32-07:00","id":1561513,"title":"","content":"There are even in-universe examples. The Baali had so many self-declared Shaitans that it eventually became more of a title for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, it's a universe where a common mental concept can create an actual entity, so the relevancy becomes more of an chicken-egg situation. The vampire Odin may have created the spirit Odin who is the ideation of the god Odin, but each one will think of themselves as the original. And it rarely matters who is right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T08:20:43-07:00","id":1561521,"title":"","content":"It becomes even more complicated if we add Godheads.<br /> <br /> Those are multiversal entities, existing simultaneously in several iterations of the world.<br /> <br /> So, if there's an Odin Godhead... How do we know if the first Odin of this universe isn't just a pressage of the Godhead's coming?<br /> <br /> Vampire Odin came to be because Odin was fated to be, even if he's the first he's byproduct of an actual god that came later rather than its origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T08:51:07-07:00","id":1561523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561513#post1561513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are even in-universe examples. The Baali had so many self-declared Shaitans that it eventually became more of a title for them.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, it's a universe where a common mental concept can create an actual entity, so the relevancy becomes more of an chicken-egg situation. The vampire Odin may have created the spirit Odin who is the ideation of the god Odin, but each one will think of themselves as the original. And it rarely matters who is right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the bit in <i>Clanbook: Baali</i> where they talk about a false Shaitan who really thinks he's the real Shaitan but is actually a puppet of Nergal. He set up a college of infernalists in Europe and then travelled so far West they hope he fell of the edge of the world. The implication being that Huitzilopochtli may be this dupe, rather than the real Nergal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T08:57:37-07:00","id":1561524,"title":"","content":"Found it. On p. 66:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Baali who currently claims the mantle truly believes that he is in fact Shaitan. This Shaitan would seem to be the product of Nergal's machinations several centuries past, but nothing more is known of his origins. The impostor first made his presence known in the city of Toledo in al-Andalus, where he was <i>Magister</i> of the infernal Black School, a college dedicated to the dark arts. Unlike Nergal, who was more interested in spreading the worship of Namtaru, this Shaitan specialized in guiding others along the path of infernalism.<br /> <br /> It took decades for other Baali to discover the impostor's whereabouts. In the meanwhile, in a frenzy of educational fervor he caught summoning rituals and true names of power to mortals and depraved Cainites alike. Before the Black College was smashed, its graduates had already spread infernalist teachings far and wide across Europe and into northern Africa.<br /> <br /> The Baali eventually destroyed the school and all of its students, but Shaitan himself escaped. The most popular story claims that he fled westward, across the sea; other tales have him returning to the Fertile Crescent. Most Baali simply hope he went too far west, fell off the edge of the world and dashed his head against the rocks below. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T16:08:37-07:00","id":1561534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561486#post1561486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third time lucky with the spam filter:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No problem. The timeline is definitely a mess and the <i>Transylvania Chronicles</i> are also riddled with date errors, even between the books in the series itself. Some plot elements also just get plain retconned in later books. For example, TC4 also says that Tremere himself had to wake up and curse both the Assamites and the Tremere <i>antitribu</i>, with the implication being that he did both at the same time or close together. But elsewhere the <i>antitribu</i> get cursed after the clan compiles the names of the suspected defectors, and the date given for the latter is different again. Similarly, TC4 says Goratrix is probably dead, and Tremere left his soul to pass on or whatever, but didn't care about protecting it. Yet <i>Nights of Prophecy</i> says Tremere keeps his soul safe in a crystal mirror, until the time he finds a suitable replacement body.<br /> <br /> <i>Clanbook: Assamite</i> came out in 1995, while TC2 was 1998, so I think the authors of TC2 just didn't read it or went with something different because they wanted to tell a particular story. But ultimately, I figure that the Treaty of Tyre wouldn't have been necessary at all if the Assamites had already been successfully cursed, so I treat it as the Convention not being enough to curse the whole clan.<br /> <br /> As another factor, the Baali Curse didn't work all that well initially, either. They had to capture Izhim abd'Azrael (and 11 others) and give him to Namtaru for it to finally spread effectively.<br /> <br /> <br /> Revised did this thing where they implied certain powerful elders might have been demons or spirits all along. Tezcatlipoca is implied to be either a vampire or spirit in VTM, but the same goes for Huitzilopochtli. Interestingly, the MTAs section on Tezcatlipoca says that Huitzilopochtli is one of his avatars, implying they're both the same being. That means Nergal maybe got retconned out of VTM for a hot second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where's that? The Tremere himself cursing the Assamites. Interpreting those events is complicated therefore i'm just compiling them and then state the different dates towards what happened.<br /> <br /> I remember the inconscintencies of TC4 and NoP, and I can't recall which came first but I do recall that TC4 was definitely not liked when it came out (nukes and stuff issue).<br /> <br /> I did state that the antitribu have different dates for the Mark of the Betrayer on the timeline.<br /> <br /> Where's the Namtaru being a thing for the curse? IIRC its only mention is Libellus Sanguinis 3. (I'll later write the entry from The Cainite Conspiracies where Izhim ur-Baal sacrifices her childe, Enkara to Namtaru if I hadn't already).<br /> <br /> Tezcatlipoca is assumed to be a wraith in shadow nature too according to Book of the Oblivion (20th anniversary), so that messes up a lot when you're trying to give sense to the Tlacique (yeah, i'm trying). On Huitzilopochtli, it's clear that Shaitan defeated the mortal warrior and became the god itself on Chaos Factor. If there is a spirit or &quot;thing&quot; beyond this, Shaitan has the power to overwhelm it. Also, Ixtab is a earthbound demon to complicate things further (book: DtF: Earthbound). The story from The Beast Within with Nezahualcoyotl is already impossible to make sense since &quot;Nezzy&quot; was already in north america before Shaitan get there (Nezzy knew Quetzalcoatl, this was around 500 aprox, though the historical day for the first ruler of the Mexica was a millennium later, and Shaitan came to the Mexica around 1000 walking through the ocean floor).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","user":"Saga","date":". 07-09-2026, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T00:02:45-07:00","id":1561557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561523#post1561523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and then travelled so far West they hope he fell of the edge of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Work as a joke, though people didn't actually thought the Earth was flat. Well, most didn't, we had Flat Earthers and they were already pretty much everything they are today.<br /> <br /> But I'm not much versed into Baali lore, why the ones in the Clanbook fight infernalists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T01:40:01-07:00","id":1561560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561557#post1561557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I'm not much versed into Baali lore, why the ones in the Clanbook fight infernalists?</div> </div> </div> </div>The short answer is internal schisms on how to use infernalism. Nergal and his line wanted to use it to awaken Namtaru and thus spread the use as much as possible, Moloch and his line would rather use it to keep the Children asleep and keep it under wraps. Both lines thought using it to enslave yourself to demons was pretty stupid. Dark Ages Baali thought themselves above infernal powers, in contrast to their modern kin. It's pretty fun contrasting the Dark Ages version of Daimonion and the modern version with that in mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T15:49:59-07:00","id":1561575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561534#post1561534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interpreting those events is complicated therefore i'm just compiling them and then state the different dates towards what happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>That approach makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561534#post1561534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's that? The Tremere himself cursing the Assamites.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I did state that the antitribu have different dates for the Mark of the Betrayer on the timeline. </div> </div> </div>Yes, you did. But it's worse than that. As far as I can see, there are actually three dates given for the curse: 1496, 16th century and 1750. I'll go through them in turn. The first two could be handwaved as the writer saying &quot;around 1500&quot;, which sort of works if you squint, but see the info below. The 18th century date has the most support.<br /> <br /> To answer your first question, though, see TC4, p. 44:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Transylvania Chronicles: The Dragon Ascendant, p. 44</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the wake of the Anarch Revolt and the Council of Thorns, <b>Tremere rouses from torpor long enough to assist in the ritual that curses the Assamites.</b> <b>He also magically brands those Tremere who do not follow the clan\u2019s dictates</b> with a telltale sigil that only true Tremere can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>A strict reading of this implies he did both at or near the same time (so probably 1496). &quot;He also...&quot; does this, rather than &quot;He later&quot; does this. It's possible he stayed awake for at least 4 years, though, and did the Rite of the Betrayers in 1500 or thereafter, making the 16th century date given elsewhere accurate. This is a bit clumsy, but technically keeps both statements true. So, it's up to you whether you list this as one date of &quot;~1500&quot; or two dates of &quot;<br /> <br /> That Tremere performed the curse himself also aligns somewhat with the original Clanbook: Tremere, p. 20:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Tremere, p. 20</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the mid-18th century, it was noticed that a number of younger Tremere had inexplicably gone missing. Only through diligent effort was it learned that Goratrix, hidden deep in the mountains of Eastern Europe, had joined with the Sabbat and was perhaps responsible for these defections. He is the head of his own covenant, House Goratrix, and his loyal antitribu followers now act as counsels and advisors to Sabbat leaders in-both the Old and New Worlds. <b>Since the discovery of House Goratrix</b>, the Tremere Councilors, led by Tremere himself, have branded the followers of Goratrix with a sigil marked on their foreheads, readily visible to any Tremere magus,</div> </div> </div> </div>A strict reading here implies it happened in or after the &quot;mid-18th century&quot;, since it says &quot;Since the discovery of House Goratrix&quot; (i.e., afterwards). This fits with a 1750 date. It also says Tremere led the 18th-century rite. Maybe he woke up again?<br /> <br /> The mid-18th century date also aligns with the date given in TC3, p. 17:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Transylvania Chronicles III: Ill Omens, p. 17</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody knows what sect you are part of just by looking at you (the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> won\u2019t have to deal with that problem until the mid-1700s), and nobody is forcing you to tell them.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again on p. 103:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Transylvania Chronicles III: Ill Omens, p. 103</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">1750: The Tremere, after three centuries of compiling a list of suspected traitors to the clan, ritually curse the <i>antitribu</i> with a symbol that all Tremere can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've already seen this date, but note that this says the ritual was performed &quot;after three centuries of compiling a list&quot;, suggesting they knew about the defections from around 1450 (likely the 1465 date when the antitribu joined the anarchs). Again, this all fits with the 1750 date.<br /> <br /> Yet, as you rightly point out in your timeline, TC2, p. 112 puts the Rite of the Betrayers in the 16th century:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Transylvania Chronicles II: Son of the Dragon, p. 112</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A rogue branch of the Tremere within the anarch ranks make its presence known. Descendants from Goratrix, these rogues seek protection from the Tremere within the ranks of the anarchs. In the 16th century, when the Sabbat forms, the Tremere antitribu are cursed (<b>much like their sire Goratrix</b>) with the mark of the traitor magically branded on their foreheads. Though invisible to normal sight, the mark is instantly noticeable by any non-Sabbat Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat usually isn't considered officially &quot;formed&quot; until the mid-16th century by most sources, which complicates the picture. But if we assume they're merely referring to the time when a bunch of anarchs refused to kowtow to the Camarilla and kept on going, then the early 16th century is still plausible. Either way, it potentially creates a third date for the curse.<br /> <br /> Note the second bit of bolded text, though. Why say this if Goratrix was cursed at the same time? This implies he was cursed earlier. The best way I've found to reconcile the dates is to assume Goratrix (and maybe a handful of others) was cursed at the same time as the Assamites, in 1496, by Tremere himself. Over the next few decades, those in-the-know within Clan Tremere use the same (or a similar) ritual to curse any other known defectors, one by one. These are probably all descendants of Goratrix, since these are the easiest &quot;missing&quot; Cainites to identify.<br /> <br /> But in 1750, the clan learns that the defectors aren't just small pockets of resistance, or even only direct childer of Goratrix, but a wide network calling itself &quot;House Goratrix&quot;. So they do the only rational thing for such a bunch of control freaks: they alter the curse they'd been using to target specific defectors (or replace it) to instead target any Tremere who partakes of the Vaulderie. Maybe Tremere woke up for this ritual, too, or maybe it was just Etrius. They probably only acted because this was the point at which the rest of the clan learned of the <i>antitribu</i>, and they had to make a big show of smacking them down.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat supported by the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat </i>(p. 81) and the previously mentioned text in the first clanbook, which both suggest the 18th century was when the main clan, as a whole, learned about the antitribu (the Inner Council and select others probably knew the whole time).<br /> <br /> PGttS technically suggests the 18th century is when the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> first joined the Sabbat, not when they were discovered, but that appears to have been retconned with TC2. Best guess? That's just when one particularly prominent wave of defectors joined in the New World, the others mostly being defectors from the Old World who joined the Sabbat during the 14th and 15th centuries. It was this second, probably larger, defection, occurring during the Camarilla\u2013Sabbat war, that tipped off the &quot;grunts&quot; of Clan Tremere and therefore required immediate action. They didn't have the time or energy to fight their own clanmates as well as the rest of the Sabbat, so tried to put a stop to it once and for all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561534#post1561534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember the inconscintencies of TC4 and NoP, and I can't recall which came first but I do recall that TC4 was definitely not liked when it came out (nukes and stuff issue).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think TC4 was published first, as NoP mentions TC4 but not the other way around. A quick check here seems to back that up: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_books\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Va...squerade_books</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561534#post1561534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's the Namtaru being a thing for the curse? IIRC its only mention is Libellus Sanguinis 3. (I'll later write the entry from The Cainite Conspiracies where Izhim ur-Baal sacrifices her childe, Enkara to Namtaru if I hadn't already).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's divided between several sources. Part of it is in <i>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology</i>, so you'll find it when you return to that. Firstly, it's noted that the curse required a sacrifice to Namtaru:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology, p. 115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Dated to 646 AD:] <b>By the time we had arrived, Izhim and his fellows had nearly been subsumed into the Hand of Namtaru which had begun to move of its own accord. </b>What we had naively believed to be the Baali\u2019s idol now seemed to literally be the demon they worshiped, buried since time immemorial beneath this cursed hilltop.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology, p. 116</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Dated to 646 AD:] <b>Then, he [Izhim] slid further into the demon\u2019s stony flesh.</b> [...] Izhim screamed my name once more. I turned to face him just in time to see his agonized face disappear within the corpus of the buried Namtaru. Weeping at my loss, I rushed forward one last time to grasp his still free hand and kiss it. <b>Then, it was ripped away to sink into the Hand which instantly solidified back into impervious basalt.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology, p. 117\u201319</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Dated to 1242 AD:] \u201cWhat you must understand, Enkara, is that <b>the Baali\u2019s ritual was\u2026 inadequate</b>. [...] The Battle of Chorazin was a trap for the Children of Haqim, one in which mortals and Baali and\u2026 prisoners were sacrificed to the Fallen One. [...] ...the Fallen One took me inside of him and conveyed me to\u2026 that other place. He\u2026 he showed me things, Enkara. He told me things. I\u2026 I had no idea. [...] Despite the Baali\u2019s best efforts, their curse was incomplete. <b>The sacrifice of so many lives aroused the Fallen One but not enough for him to grant the boon they requested. The Fallen One wanted more. And what he wanted was something only I could give him. You see, of all the Children offered up that night, I was the only one who truly, truly loved someone else. You.</b> [...] \u201cI, Izhim, called Thrice-Blessed, childe of Anath, grand-childe of Haqim the Hunter, offer freely my name, my allegiance, and my one true love in accordance with our agreement. <b>Let the contract be fulfilled.</b>\u201d [...] \u201cIt is done,\u201d he said solemnly. <b>\u201cThe sacrifice is accepted. The Blood-Curse which was but a trickle through the warrior caste will become a flood. </b>It will taint them all and pass thence to the other castes. The Children will become cannibal-monsters who hunt not for justice but merely to satiate their lust for diablerie. The other clans will despise the Children and, in time, seek their destruction.<b> Thus is the vengeance of the Baali fulfilled.\u201d</b> [...] \u201cIzhim Thrice-Blessed is gone, my Beautiful Weapon. My name is Izhim ur-Baal. And at last, I am free.\u201d With that, he turned and walked away. Enkara screamed once more before she was lost within the Hand of Namtaru. Izhim ur-Baal departed and passed into history.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Libellus Sanguinis 3: Wolves at the Door, p. 53\u201354</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">During the Baali retreat, tragedy befell the warriors. One of the greatest among them, the ancient Izhim abd\u2019Azrae1, was struck down and taken captive. [...] He had been no sacrifice, but rather the focal point of a ritual that struck at the very heart of the clan. [...] <b>His blood was strong and old </b><b>enough to serve as a focal point for a curse that is still </b><b>creeping across the warrior caste</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back to <i>Clanbook: Assamite Revised</i> and the Anarch Revolt:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Assamite Revised, p. 23</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Chorazin burned, the combined strength of the Children of Haqim overwhelmed the last defenders of the temple. Inside, they found but one survivor of those who the Baali had taken prisoner. He gasped out a fearful tale, one that few gave credence for months to come. The Baali had said to him, \u201cAs you thirst for our blood, so shall you hunger for all blood for all time.\u201d <b>Then they had used the captured warriors as a focus for a curse that intensified their ancient craving a thousandfold.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>So it's pretty clear that the Baali Curse was first imposed in 646 AD, using Izhim abd'Azrael and a dozen other Baali as sacrifices to curse the whole clan. But it's also fairly clear this didn't fully work, and it was only after Izhim ur-Baal sacrificed Enkara to Namtaru in 1242 that the Curse actually spread throughout the majority of the clan.<br /> <br /> [QUOTE]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clanbook: Assamite Revised, p. 26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Several of the sorcerers supporting these warriors [the Unconquered] believed they had found a means by which the Tremere spell might be broken. On their word, <b>these so-called Unconquered set forth from Alamut to journey to the hell-city where the infernalists had cursed their line</b>. Although the Baali were little but a distant memory by now, <b>the sorcerers believed that the place from which that curse had sprung might yield clues to the breaking of this new one</b>. [...] While <b>the </b><b>sorcerers were able to reawaken one of the cursed altars</b> and strip the power of the Tremere blood from their own small band, <b>they also awakened something else that had </b><b>lain buried beneath Chorazin for nearly a millennium</b>. No two survivors of that night tell the same tale of the bloodstorm that came after, but at its end, every vizier and sorcerer who had ridden with the Unconquered was destroyed, the secret of their success lost with them. <b>The </b><b>eldest surviving warrior, Izhim abd\u2019Azrael, led his tattered followers forth from the ruins of that blighted city </b><b>in search of a new home.</b> In time, they joined the nascent Sabbat, accepting the name \u201cAssamite <i>antitribu</i>\u201d and the chance to kill Cainites of the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Children of the Night, p. 13</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>He [Izhim ur-Baal] rode with the great</b><b>est of their companies to the forgotten city of Chorazin</b>; in time, <b>strengthened by forbidden tutelage</b> and the passage of centuries, he rose to rule them [the Unconquered]. [...] His motivations in this matter and others remain a mystery \u2014 common accusations range from simple lust for power to subversive agendas to <b>otherworldly alliances forged in his youth</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Ur-Shulgi is not the only Assamite with ties with the Baali. It's also strongly implied that Namtaru was the thing the Unconquered reawakened in Chorazin while removing the Tremere Curse and it's also implied the Curse was broken because they replaced it with the old Baali Curse. And who should be leading them all immediately after this happened? Izhim ur-Baal, the same Assamite who was captured to spread the Baali Curse in the first place (in 646 AD), and the Assamite responsible for helping it spread further in 1242.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T11:22:08-07:00","id":1561610,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=adambeyoncelowe;n1561575]<br /> <br /> That approach makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, you did. But it's worse than that. As far as I can see, there are actually three dates given for the curse: 1496, 16th century and 1750. I'll go through them in turn. The first two could be handwaved as the writer saying &quot;around 1500&quot;, which sort of works if you squint, but see the info below. The 18th century date has the most support.<br /> <br /> To answer your first question, though, see TC4, p. 44:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A strict reading of this implies he did both at or near the same time (so probably 1496). &quot;He also...&quot; does this, rather than &quot;He later&quot; does this. It's possible he stayed awake for at least 4 years, though, and did the Rite of the Betrayers in 1500 or thereafter, making the 16th century date given elsewhere accurate. This is a bit clumsy, but technically keeps both statements true. So, it's up to you whether you list this as one date of &quot;~1500&quot; or two dates of &quot;<br /> <br /> That Tremere performed the curse himself also aligns somewhat with the original Clanbook: Tremere, p. 20:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A strict reading here implies it happened in or after the &quot;mid-18th century&quot;, since it says &quot;Since the discovery of House Goratrix&quot; (i.e., afterwards). This fits with a 1750 date. It also says Tremere led the 18th-century rite. Maybe he woke up again?<br /> <br /> The mid-18th century date also aligns with the date given in TC3, p. 17:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And again on p. 103:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You've already seen this date, but note that this says the ritual was performed &quot;after three centuries of compiling a list&quot;, suggesting they knew about the defections from around 1450 (likely the 1465 date when the antitribu joined the anarchs). Again, this all fits with the 1750 date.<br /> <br /> Yet, as you rightly point out in your timeline, TC2, p. 112 puts the Rite of the Betrayers in the 16th century:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat usually isn't considered officially &quot;formed&quot; until the mid-16th century by most sources, which complicates the picture. But if we assume they're merely referring to the time when a bunch of anarchs refused to kowtow to the Camarilla and kept on going, then the early 16th century is still plausible. Either way, it potentially creates a third date for the curse.<br /> <br /> Note the second bit of bolded text, though. Why say this if Goratrix was cursed at the same time? This implies he was cursed earlier. The best way I've found to reconcile the dates is to assume Goratrix (and maybe a handful of others) was cursed at the same time as the Assamites, in 1496, by Tremere himself. Over the next few decades, those in-the-know within Clan Tremere use the same (or a similar) ritual to curse any other known defectors, one by one. These are probably all descendants of Goratrix, since these are the easiest &quot;missing&quot; Cainites to identify.<br /> <br /> But in 1750, the clan learns that the defectors aren't just small pockets of resistance, or even only direct childer of Goratrix, but a wide network calling itself &quot;House Goratrix&quot;. So they do the only rational thing for such a bunch of control freaks: they alter the curse they'd been using to target specific defectors (or replace it) to instead target any Tremere who partakes of the Vaulderie. Maybe Tremere woke up for this ritual, too, or maybe it was just Etrius. They probably only acted because this was the point at which the rest of the clan learned of the <i>antitribu</i>, and they had to make a big show of smacking them down.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat supported by the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat </i>(p. 81) and the previously mentioned text in the first clanbook, which both suggest the 18th century was when the main clan, as a whole, learned about the antitribu (the Inner Council and select others probably knew the whole time).<br /> <br /> PGttS technically suggests the 18th century is when the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> first joined the Sabbat, not when they were discovered, but that appears to have been retconned with TC2. Best guess? That's just when one particularly prominent wave of defectors joined in the New World, the others mostly being defectors from the Old World who joined the Sabbat during the 14th and 15th centuries. It was this second, probably larger, defection, occurring during the Camarilla\u2013Sabbat war, that tipped off the &quot;grunts&quot; of Clan Tremere and therefore required immediate action. They didn't have the time or energy to fight their own clanmates as well as the rest of the Sabbat, so tried to put a stop to it once and for all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think TC4 was published first, as NoP mentions TC4 but not the other way around. A quick check here seems to back that up: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_books\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Va...squerade_books</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's divided between several sources. Part of it is in <i>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology</i>, so you'll find it when you return to that. Firstly, it's noted that the curse required a sacrifice to Namtaru:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Back to <i>Clanbook: Assamite Revised</i> and the Anarch Revolt:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it's pretty clear that the Baali Curse was first imposed in 646 AD, using Izhim abd'Azrael and a dozen other Baali as sacrifices to curse the whole clan. But it's also fairly clear this didn't fully work, and it was only after Izhim ur-Baal sacrificed Enkara to Namtaru in 1242 that the Curse actually spread throughout the majority of the clan.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, Ur-Shulgi is not the only Assamite with ties with the Baali. It's also strongly implied that Namtaru was the thing the Unconquered reawakened in Chorazin while removing the Tremere Curse and it's also implied the Curse was broken because they replaced it with the old Baali Curse. And who should be leading them all immediately after this happened? Izhim ur-Baal, the same Assamite who was captured to spread the Baali Curse in the first place (in 646 AD), and the Assamite responsible for helping it spread further in 1242.<br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div>This is all pretty useful, thanks.<br /> <br /> On the Assamite curse, I recall that ur-Shulgi was supposed to be the &quot;third Baali&quot;, the one Shaitan and Nergal never spoke about, and the original storyline from Clanbook Assamite revised (that got left out) supported this. It would be weird that a creature that could undo the Tremere curse as soon as it got out of torpor couldn't undo a curse of its own clan. Perhaps Haqim embraced him on that intention, to betray his own clan, and therefore barely learning Daimoinon (which I believe is part of the curse). Having Izhim ur-Baal summoned would make a lot of sense since he was the catalyst of the curse itself. That always left me the question of what was Caine's original curse on the Assamites if their hunger for vitae was placed by the Baali? I believe it was the blackness on their skin. Now, why is al-Ashrad the only one left uncursed?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T13:59:11-07:00","id":1561614,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Saga;n1561610]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561575#post1561575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That approach makes the most sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, you did. But it's worse than that. As far as I can see, there are actually three dates given for the curse: 1496, 16th century and 1750. I'll go through them in turn. The first two could be handwaved as the writer saying &quot;around 1500&quot;, which sort of works if you squint, but see the info below. The 18th century date has the most support.<br /> <br /> To answer your first question, though, see TC4, p. 44:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A strict reading of this implies he did both at or near the same time (so probably 1496). &quot;He also...&quot; does this, rather than &quot;He later&quot; does this. It's possible he stayed awake for at least 4 years, though, and did the Rite of the Betrayers in 1500 or thereafter, making the 16th century date given elsewhere accurate. This is a bit clumsy, but technically keeps both statements true. So, it's up to you whether you list this as one date of &quot;~1500&quot; or two dates of &quot;<br /> <br /> That Tremere performed the curse himself also aligns somewhat with the original Clanbook: Tremere, p. 20:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A strict reading here implies it happened in or after the &quot;mid-18th century&quot;, since it says &quot;Since the discovery of House Goratrix&quot; (i.e., afterwards). This fits with a 1750 date. It also says Tremere led the 18th-century rite. Maybe he woke up again?<br /> <br /> The mid-18th century date also aligns with the date given in TC3, p. 17:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And again on p. 103:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You've already seen this date, but note that this says the ritual was performed &quot;after three centuries of compiling a list&quot;, suggesting they knew about the defections from around 1450 (likely the 1465 date when the antitribu joined the anarchs). Again, this all fits with the 1750 date.<br /> <br /> Yet, as you rightly point out in your timeline, TC2, p. 112 puts the Rite of the Betrayers in the 16th century:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Sabbat usually isn't considered officially &quot;formed&quot; until the mid-16th century by most sources, which complicates the picture. But if we assume they're merely referring to the time when a bunch of anarchs refused to kowtow to the Camarilla and kept on going, then the early 16th century is still plausible. Either way, it potentially creates a third date for the curse.<br /> <br /> Note the second bit of bolded text, though. Why say this if Goratrix was cursed at the same time? This implies he was cursed earlier. The best way I've found to reconcile the dates is to assume Goratrix (and maybe a handful of others) was cursed at the same time as the Assamites, in 1496, by Tremere himself. Over the next few decades, those in-the-know within Clan Tremere use the same (or a similar) ritual to curse any other known defectors, one by one. These are probably all descendants of Goratrix, since these are the easiest &quot;missing&quot; Cainites to identify.<br /> <br /> But in 1750, the clan learns that the defectors aren't just small pockets of resistance, or even only direct childer of Goratrix, but a wide network calling itself &quot;House Goratrix&quot;. So they do the only rational thing for such a bunch of control freaks: they alter the curse they'd been using to target specific defectors (or replace it) to instead target any Tremere who partakes of the Vaulderie. Maybe Tremere woke up for this ritual, too, or maybe it was just Etrius. They probably only acted because this was the point at which the rest of the clan learned of the <i>antitribu</i>, and they had to make a big show of smacking them down.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat supported by the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat </i>(p. 81) and the previously mentioned text in the first clanbook, which both suggest the 18th century was when the main clan, as a whole, learned about the antitribu (the Inner Council and select others probably knew the whole time).<br /> <br /> PGttS technically suggests the 18th century is when the Tremere <i>antitribu</i> first joined the Sabbat, not when they were discovered, but that appears to have been retconned with TC2. Best guess? That's just when one particularly prominent wave of defectors joined in the New World, the others mostly being defectors from the Old World who joined the Sabbat during the 14th and 15th centuries. It was this second, probably larger, defection, occurring during the Camarilla\u2013Sabbat war, that tipped off the &quot;grunts&quot; of Clan Tremere and therefore required immediate action. They didn't have the time or energy to fight their own clanmates as well as the rest of the Sabbat, so tried to put a stop to it once and for all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think TC4 was published first, as NoP mentions TC4 but not the other way around. A quick check here seems to back that up: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampire:_The_Masquerade_books\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Va...squerade_books</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It's divided between several sources. Part of it is in <i>The Cainite Conspiracies Anthology</i>, so you'll find it when you return to that. Firstly, it's noted that the curse required a sacrifice to Namtaru:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Back to <i>Clanbook: Assamite Revised</i> and the Anarch Revolt:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it's pretty clear that the Baali Curse was first imposed in 646 AD, using Izhim abd'Azrael and a dozen other Baali as sacrifices to curse the whole clan. But it's also fairly clear this didn't fully work, and it was only after Izhim ur-Baal sacrificed Enkara to Namtaru in 1242 that the Curse actually spread throughout the majority of the clan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is all pretty useful, thanks.<br /> <br /> On the Assamite curse, I recall that ur-Shulgi was supposed to be the &quot;third Baali&quot;, the one Shaitan and Nergal never spoke about, and the original storyline from Clanbook Assamite revised (that got left out) supported this. It would be weird that a creature that could undo the Tremere curse as soon as it got out of torpor couldn't undo a curse of its own clan. Perhaps Haqim embraced him on that intention, to betray his own clan, and therefore barely learning Daimoinon (which I believe is part of the curse). Having Izhim ur-Baal summoned would make a lot of sense since he was the catalyst of the curse itself. That always left me the question of what was Caine's original curse on the Assamites if their hunger for vitae was placed by the Baali? I believe it was the blackness on their skin. Now, why is al-Ashrad the only one left uncursed?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Al-Ashrad's sire is Ur-Shulgi, which could imply that neither of them are Assamites. Interestingly, Izhim ur-Baal.apparently came out of Namtaru's hand with bleached hair and pale skin, despite being blackened with age before. Which... Yeah. There's clearly a link between pale-skinned &quot;Assamites&quot; and Baali influence.<br /> <br /> Ur-Shulgi does appear to have been a plant\u2014Embraced to rally the Baali together. He appears to have been the Slave Boy of Baali myth (e.g., per the original VTDA Companion). He was almost certainly wicked or marked for wickedness to begin with (the cut Ur-Shulgi myth implies he was something like a Widderslainte, until Haqim tore the evil out of him). Whether he's just a kid with black and white views of the world (and evil in the regular Kindred way) or is something especially evil (in a Baali sense) is up for debate, but the fact he left the Baali Curse in place means he thinks it serves a purpose\u2014whether to cleanse the world of other Kindred, to fatten Haqim when he finally awakens, or to serve his Baali masters is unknown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T17:01:55-07:00","id":1561745,"title":"","content":"A couple more additions:<ul><li>Caine's Chosen (p. 9) puts the start of the First Sabbat Civil War as 1767, with its peak in 1785. This is backed up by MCbN (p. 21). MCbN says it started winding down in 1793 (&quot;one pack at a time&quot;), so it's a low ramping down until the Purchase Pact.</li> <li>GC3 (p.13) suggests it started with Shay's Rebellion in 1786. The wording is vague enough that it could just be when the civil war spread from the Americas to Europe. The same page also implies there is a Sabbat Civil War still raging by 1848, but I think this is the Second Sabbat Civil War (see further down). 2e books sometimes behave as if there was one Sabbat Civil War, even when they've said there were multiple in the same book.</li> <li>Caine's Chosen (p. 18) says Dastur Anosh went to America to help stop the war and then disappeared during it. V20 CotR (p. 64) has him come to America much earlier and disappear in 1766. The First Sabbat Civil War is said to have broken out &quot;shortly thereafter&quot;, which seems to confirm 1767.</li> <li>Clanbook: Lasombra Revised (p. 35) suggests it started in the late 1790s, which is ludicrous, much like the other dates in the book.</li> <li>Caine's Chosen (p. 20) says the Sabbat Inquisition complained about the Black Hand before the First Civil War &quot;started in earnest&quot;, but attributes this organisation to Mon\u00e7ada, Nahir, and others. This is interesting because, as you note, CotN says Black Wallace joins the Inquisition in 1780\u2014well before its official founding in 1804. But the same page of Caine's Chosen also says no Inquisitors set foot in the Americas until 1808, which implies there was a Sabbat Inquisition in Europe and that the 1804 founding was only for the American branch. Presumably they went to Europe to train up between 1804 and 1808, and then arrived in 1808 in Peru with Charles Delmare per Caine's Chosen.</li> <li>GC3 has a whole adventure based in 1848, and the Sabbat internecine squabbling is a big part of that. So, the Second Sabbat Civil War has either already started or is beginning to start.</li> <li>MCbN (p. 24) puts the first &quot;rumblings&quot; of the Second Sabbat Civil War around the time of Santa Anna's capture (22 April 1836) and his signing of the Treaties of Velasco on (14 May 1836). It states the Lasombra and Tzimisce began &quot;drawing lines in the sand&quot; around the time of the Mexico Cessation (2 February 1848), which fits GC3. In GC3 (pp. 29, 80\u201382), Doctor Streck leads the attacks on Paris and London in 1848 (Lady Vadislava having attacked London Toreador earlier). This was part of a campaign that also targeted Vienna, Milan, and Berlin, but which was unpopular among Lady Astor of London, who was set to become archbishop but wanted to take things much slower. This establishes the intense rivalries between elders prior to the over violence of the Second Sabbat Civil War.</li> <li>MCbN (still p. 24) also states that Gorchist pulls the fighting back from the brink several times, with the aid of the Black Hand, but keeps referring to it as a localised conflict. So arguably, this is still only the precursor to the war proper.</li> <li>The same page gives us another fixed date: Gorchist is assassinated on the eve of the French invasion of Mexico City, which dates it to 9 June 1863. After this, the war begins &quot;in earnest&quot;.</li> <li>Montreal by Night (p. 84) says the Conference of Caine in 1910 was a major step towards ending the Second Sabbat Civil War, so this fits. That conference took part at the same time as the Eucharistic Conference (7\u201311 September 1910). The book says the Litany is reopened &quot;every summer&quot; as a result, but apparently Canada's summer does include early September (June Solstice to the September Equinox), so that also works out as a regular anniversary event.</li> <li>The sources all agree the Second Civil War ended in 1933 with the signing of the revised Core of Milan, helmed by Galbraith per MCbN (26\u201327), but MCbN (p. 6) makes a goof and suggests Galbraith claimed the regency at the end of the Third Sabbat Civil War, which is clearly a mistake.</li> <li>Of course, the revised Code of Milan still carries Gorchist's name, despite him having met Final Death 70 years prior. This is clearly an error, but one that's sort of been retconned by saying the Code published in 1933 was only a revised version. This implies Gorchist signed the original version, or perhaps drafted the revised version before he died, but only Galbraith got it over the line. A final possibility is that it invokes Gorchist's name as the last legitimate regent of the sect, so it's like a blessing (&quot;In the name of...&quot;, etc.).</li> </ul>So, I think we can safely say the dates are:<ul><li>First Sabbat Civil War: 1767 for the start (1785/1786 for the peak); 1803 for the end.</li> <li>Second Sabbat Civil War: Between 1836 and 1848 for the early conflicts (which may or may not count as part of the war); 9 June 1863 for the &quot;official&quot; start date; 1910 for when things start to calm down; 1933 for the end.</li> <li>Third Sabbat Civil War: Latter half of 1957.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Clarify 07-16-2026, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-15T17:18:18-07:00","id":1561746,"title":"","content":"Also, a correction. You have:<ul><li>&quot;The Navigators pack assist the creation of the Sabbat Inquisition. There, Santiago DeSoto meets the Shepherds of Caine and then travels to Montreal.&quot; (MbN, p. 95)</li> </ul>But actually, that page says:<ul><li>&quot;DeSoto <i>learned of </i>the Shepherds <i>after the coven </i>assisted in the creation of the Inquisition. [...] DeSoto went to Montreal - under the cover of trading information with the Librarians - to <i>insinuate himself into</i> the highly influential Shepherds and their Inquisition.&quot;</li> </ul>I.e., &quot;the coven [that] assisted in the creation of the Inquisition&quot; was the Shepherds. Otherwise it would be something like: &quot;DeSoto <i>met</i> the Shepherds <i>when the Navigators</i> assisted in the creation of the Inquisition.&quot;<br /> <br /> Also, the fact he moved there to &quot;insinuate himself&quot; among the Shepherds and Inquisition implies it was already created by that point. If you read further, he only becomes an Inquisitor <i>after</i> training with the Shepherds, so the timeline is pretty clear. But it's an easy mistake to make when taking notes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-16T11:18:56-07:00","id":1561777,"title":"","content":"Another one:<ul><li>~1550: Lucita meets Lambach Ruthven in Lenapehoking (modern day New York City) before the Code of Milan went out and learns of the tale in which the Tzimisce founder survived his diablerie. [LT2-S, pg. 126]</li> </ul>This can't be accurate. If you turn the next page, if says:<ul><li>&quot;I laughed at him, in fact, and asked if he expected the founder to show up on the next train, since we were visiting in one of the subway tunnels.&quot; [LT2-S, Pg. 126]</li> </ul>But the NYC subway wasn't opened to the public until 27 October 1904. Even if we factor in the four years required to build it, she can't have met Lambach earlier than 1900. Clearly, when she says she &quot;met him just once, in New York City, shortly before the original Code of Milan went out&quot;, she must be talking about the revised Code of Milan, which was drafted in NYC. This puts their meeting somewhere between 1904 and 1933.<br /> <br /> The lore of <i>The</i> <i>Code of Milan</i> is another of those tangled messes. According to the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat</i> (p. 97), the Code was penned &quot;during the great Camarilla\u2013Sabbat Jyhads of the early years&quot;, when &quot;a civil war split the Sabbat&quot; (presumably the First Sabbat Civil War, but it could potentially just be a smaller precursor). It was signed in Milan in order to end the conflict, meaning it occupies the same narrative space as the Purchase Pact (which first appeared in GttS, AFAICS). Frankly, adding the Purchase Pact is probably the thing that messed it up the most. It also says those on the Path of Honourable Accord follow a version of this Code that was massively expanded between the First and Second Sabbat Civil Wars, and that version is likely no longer the same Code people mean when they talk about the original.<br /> <br /> According to the <i>Storytellers Handbook to be Sabbat</i> (p. 43), it's existed since the Sabbat began in one form another, but only &quot;gained acceptance&quot; after &quot;the Sabbat Civil War&quot; (it doesn't say which). Like MCbN and GttS, however, it says the Code was &quot;revised&quot; in New York, so this presumably refers to the revised Code published in 1933 (hence, at the end of the Second Sabbat Civil War). It also says this version is <i>shorter</i> than the original, was revised because of the efforts of the Black Hand (there's no separation of powers here!), and that many packs recite it at the start of their <i>esbats</i>, making it &quot;a creed now than a set of laws&quot;.<br /> <br /> <i>Montreal by Night </i>(p. 73) only mentions it once, as the (clearly misspelled) &quot;Code of Milian&quot;. But it honestly would've been better to have two different codes with different names.<br /> <br /> <i>Clanbook: Lasombra Revised</i> says the revised Code probably isn't actually reflective of the original Code at all (p. 35), but is rather a &quot;consensus statement&quot; between the Black Angels and everyone else. Giangaleazzo apparently burned the original, so I would look to the date of his &quot;coronation&quot; as Prince for the date of the original draft. He may have allowed the document to be written there prior to his public defection.<br /> <br /> According to <i>Chaining the Beast</i> (pp. 56\u201359)\u200b, the tenets of the Path of Honourable Accord go back to the Path of Chivalry, with its principles dating to 1150 or earlier, but the tarot motif in the Code dates its final compilation to much later. The tarot was invented in Italy between 1425 and 1442, but their use in divination originates in the 18th century. That gives us 1425 as the earliest date for the longer Code.<br /> <br /> I think those are the main references I can find. I guess it's feasible that the Purchase Pact came first, ending the war, and Gorchist promised to document the <i>Code of Milan</i> afterwards as a sop to the traditionalists. Alternatively, maybe the name was simply recycled from the original, apocryphal text to give it more respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T17:00:02-07:00","id":1561856,"title":"","content":"I love that discussion. Also because it's a perfect example what a mess WoD lore became, even in the span of 13 years that WW had to print the original 3 editions. As messy as it is the details of the lore and metaplot are still a fascinating topic for discussions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T23:35:02-07:00","id":1561876,"title":"","content":"Indeed it's always good to discuss how messy lore can become when the IP continues to grow and develop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T01:36:42-07:00","id":1561878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561856#post1561856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love that discussion. Also because it's a perfect example what a mess WoD lore became, even in the span of 13 years that WW had to print the original 3 editions. As messy as it is the details of the lore and metaplot are still a fascinating topic for discussions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you can tell, I'm a little obsessed with the lore right now. I've been developing a Sabbat guide for V20 (mostly for myself; maybe for STV one day), which involved creating a whole timeline of the sect from the first stirrings of the Anarch Revolt and a little before. (I basically start during the War of Princes, since that's when the Inquisition begins being active.)<br /> <br /> After fleshing it out with every detail I could find about the Sabbat, I then began filling in the gaps for things to add plot hooks, explain things that didn't make sense, or give more specifics for individual events. E.g., there's lots written about the Sabbat Civil Wars in Mexico, and sometimes the US, but there's practically nothing about what happened in Europe during these times.<br /> <br /> The messiness of the lore really does make it feel like you're studying real-world history, though, because even that is widely disagreed upon in many cases. Not just in terms of whether event x happened on date a or b, but also in terms of what event x even means and whether event y was also an influence.<br /> <br /> Filling the gaps in can create new storytelling opportunities if you like that sort of thing. E.g., Melinda Galbraith (no given surname at the time) is said to be &quot;a fourth generation Lasombra&quot; in the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat </i>(1992), where it describes her as &quot;a ruthless manipulator who used assassination and blackmail to gain control of the sect; however, she has proven time and time again to be an outstanding leader&quot; (p. 19). It also says there have been four regents (further up on p. 19) and &quot;all but one of the Regents&quot; have been Lasombra (p. 61).<br /> <br /> The <i>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat </i>(1993) finally gives her a surname, and says there are two archbishops beneath her in Mexico City, since the city is so huge (p. 35). It's said Mexico City is rivalled only by NYC for the power of its vampire inhabitants. The book also says Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> Loyalists dislike the revised <i>Code of Milan</i>, since they don't think the regent responsible for it had the authority.<br /> <br /> In hindsight, that little line his actually makes the apparent contradictions gel slightly better, since Gorchist's death in 1863 (per MCbN, p. 24) means he couldn't possibly have been the one signing the Code in 1933, even though it bears his name and says it is his decree (its opening line states &quot;by the solemn word of Regent Gorchist&quot;). Since MCbN established that Galbraith unveiled the signed Code in 1933 and then declared herself regent, this prior bit of information retroactively suggests she was laying claim to Gorchist's authority a full 70 years after his Final Death. She really didn't have the authority to make it official, and Gorchist was dead, so he didn't either! What was an error created by later books (Gorchist signing a document after his death) can become plausible again when you comb back over the old details\u2014to get things done, Galbraith had to invoke the dead regent to authorise herself as the new regent. This is perfect fuel for Loyalists to continue to challenge the Status Quo.<br /> <br /> In<i> The Chaos Factor</i> (1994), Melinda Galbraith is retconned to be the childe of Helena, and is only the cardinal of Mexico City (later books ignore her demotion, but you can assume she's regent <i>and</i> cardinal if it helps). This is when she becomes a fifth generation Toreador <i>antitribu</i>. This ostensibly creates another problem, since prior books established her as Lasombra, except that MCbN also reveals that the Lasombra kept out all the other clans from Mexico, Hispaniola, and most of the New World until at least 1519 (p. 16). Meaning Melinda and Helena may simply have posed as Lasombra to allow them to travel with Cort\u00e9s to Hispaniola in 1504. Once again, with a bit of quick thinking, a retcon can make a little bit more sense. (Her generation is still out by one, but if she doesn't tell anyone who her sire is, it makes sense that they might assume she's fourth generation. If you like, it could alternatively mean she's committed diablerie. <i>Mexico City by Night</i>, p. 17, says Huitzilopochtli was diablerised, so what if that's when Galbraith became fourth generation? Wait, she ate Shaitan?! Plot twist!)<br /> <br /> It does, however, create other issues, in that her backstory now makes her Spanish (Galbraith is a Scottish surname), and her first name comes from the 19th century, not the 12th when she was sired. Maybe she made the name up, though, to distance herself from her past. This is sort of supported by a typo in CF, where they twice call her &quot;Marie&quot; instead of Melinda (both on p. 17). So maybe Marie was her original name (or more likely Maria)? A Spanish Cainite called Maria could plausibly fit in with the Lasombra, especially if she and her sire have bucketloads of Presence and Dominate. To also fit her portrayal as Lasombra, Galbraith has Dominate 8, Obtenebration 5, and Potence 7 in CF, so that sells the lie.<br /> <br /> There's still the issue of the regents. Once Gorchist is said to be Tzimisce, it means all three of the other regents must be Lasombra. But now that we've established how she snuck into New Spain, it could just be the case that most simply believe Galbraith to be Lasombra. <i>New York by Night</i> addresses this by repeatedly suggesting most Sabbat Cainites (and even Camarilla Kindred) assume whoever is in charge is Lasombra, and the Lasombra don't correct them because it suits them to have everyone believe they're in charge (pp. 17, 18, 25, and indirectly on pp. 20 and 21).<br /> <br /> And now I immediately want to start writing up the other two regents and who they were! Do they still have loyal followers who blame their successors for their Final Deaths? PGttS (p. 19) and <i>Guide to the Sabbat</i> (p. 152) imply that's how most regents got their position, after all...<br /> <br /> Of course, since the books often contradict themselves, it creates an implicit invitation to do that ourselves. So you don't even need to try and make it make sense\u2014you can just pick the bits you like and ignore the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T01:42:07-07:00","id":1561879,"title":"","content":"I forgot to say: MCbN (p. 113) says there's no archbishop in the city &quot;because the regent fills that role&quot;. Since CF said there were previously two, this could also create a new story hook\u2014what happened to the two missing archbishops? Did someone kill them? Did Melinda eat them, too? Did she just remove them because she wanted to centralise the Sabbat's power even more? Did they die in a Crusade or by assassination (hello, Tlacique!)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-18T03:13:27-07:00","id":1561882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561878#post1561878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As you can tell, I'm a little obsessed with the lore right now. I've been developing a Sabbat guide for V20 (mostly for myself; maybe for STV one day), which involved creating a whole timeline of the sect from the first stirrings of the Anarch Revolt and a little before. (I basically start during the War of Princes, since that's when the Inquisition begins being active.)<br /> <br /> After fleshing it out with every detail I could find about the Sabbat, I then began filling in the gaps for things to add plot hooks, explain things that didn't make sense, or give more specifics for individual events. E.g., there's lots written about the Sabbat Civil Wars in Mexico, and sometimes the US, but there's practically nothing about what happened in Europe during these times.<br /> <br /> The messiness of the lore really does make it feel like you're studying real-world history, though, because even that is widely disagreed upon in many cases. Not just in terms of whether event x happened on date a or b, but also in terms of what event x even means and whether event y was also an influence.<br /> <br /> Filling the gaps in can create new storytelling opportunities if you like that sort of thing. E.g., Melinda Galbraith (no given surname at the time) is said to be &quot;a fourth generation Lasombra&quot; in the <i>Players Guide to the Sabbat </i>(1992), where it describes her as &quot;a ruthless manipulator who used assassination and blackmail to gain control of the sect; however, she has proven time and time again to be an outstanding leader&quot; (p. 19). It also says there have been four regents (further up on p. 19) and &quot;all but one of the Regents&quot; have been Lasombra (p. 61).<br /> <br /> The <i>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat </i>(1993) finally gives her a surname, and says there are two archbishops beneath her in Mexico City, since the city is so huge (p. 35). It's said Mexico City is rivalled only by NYC for the power of its vampire inhabitants. The book also says Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> Loyalists dislike the revised <i>Code of Milan</i>, since they don't think the regent responsible for it had the authority.<br /> <br /> In hindsight, that little line his actually makes the apparent contradictions gel slightly better, since Gorchist's death in 1863 (per MCbN, p. 24) means he couldn't possibly have been the one signing the Code in 1933, even though it bears his name and says it is his decree (its opening line states &quot;by the solemn word of Regent Gorchist&quot;). Since MCbN established that Galbraith unveiled the signed Code in 1933 and then declared herself regent, this prior bit of information retroactively suggests she was laying claim to Gorchist's authority a full 70 years after his Final Death. She really didn't have the authority to make it official, and Gorchist was dead, so he didn't either! What was an error created by later books (Gorchist signing a document after his death) can become plausible again when you comb back over the old details\u2014to get things done, Galbraith had to invoke the dead regent to authorise herself as the new regent. This is perfect fuel for Loyalists to continue to challenge the Status Quo.<br /> <br /> In<i> The Chaos Factor</i> (1994), Melinda Galbraith is retconned to be the childe of Helena, and is only the cardinal of Mexico City (later books ignore her demotion, but you can assume she's regent <i>and</i> cardinal if it helps). This is when she becomes a fifth generation Toreador <i>antitribu</i>. This ostensibly creates another problem, since prior books established her as Lasombra, except that MCbN also reveals that the Lasombra kept out all the other clans from Mexico, Hispaniola, and most of the New World until at least 1519 (p. 16). Meaning Melinda and Helena may simply have posed as Lasombra to allow them to travel with Cort\u00e9s to Hispaniola in 1504. Once again, with a bit of quick thinking, a retcon can make a little bit more sense. (Her generation is still out by one, but if she doesn't tell anyone who her sire is, it makes sense that they might assume she's fourth generation. If you like, it could alternatively mean she's committed diablerie. <i>Mexico City by Night</i>, p. 17, says Huitzilopochtli was diablerised, so what if that's when Galbraith became fourth generation? Wait, she ate Shaitan?! Plot twist!)<br /> <br /> It does, however, create other issues, in that her backstory now makes her Spanish (Galbraith is a Scottish surname), and her first name comes from the 19th century, not the 12th when she was sired. Maybe she made the name up, though, to distance herself from her past. This is sort of supported by a typo in CF, where they twice call her &quot;Marie&quot; instead of Melinda (both on p. 17). So maybe Marie was her original name (or more likely Maria)? A Spanish Cainite called Maria could plausibly fit in with the Lasombra, especially if she and her sire have bucketloads of Presence and Dominate. To also fit her portrayal as Lasombra, Galbraith has Dominate 8, Obtenebration 5, and Potence 7 in CF, so that sells the lie.<br /> <br /> There's still the issue of the regents. Once Gorchist is said to be Tzimisce, it means all three of the other regents must be Lasombra. But now that we've established how she snuck into New Spain, it could just be the case that most simply believe Galbraith to be Lasombra. <i>New York by Night</i> addresses this by repeatedly suggesting most Sabbat Cainites (and even Camarilla Kindred) assume whoever is in charge is Lasombra, and the Lasombra don't correct them because it suits them to have everyone believe they're in charge (pp. 17, 18, 25, and indirectly on pp. 20 and 21).<br /> <br /> And now I immediately want to start writing up the other two regents and who they were! Do they still have loyal followers who blame their successors for their Final Deaths? PGttS (p. 19) and <i>Guide to the Sabbat</i> (p. 152) imply that's how most regents got their position, after all...<br /> <br /> Of course, since the books often contradict themselves, it creates an implicit invitation to do that ourselves. So you don't even need to try and make it make sense\u2014you can just pick the bits you like and ignore the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh right, I even forgot she was Lasombra in the Chaos Factor. I just remember us running the Sabbat (yes, I am a fan of clan Toreador). Her posing as Lasombra makes sense even if it is a retcon (I don't think it is ever explicitly mentioned in the books), vampires pretending to be other clans is nothing unheard of. <br /> <br /> And I know what you are saying about the regents. I was reading through Courts of the Damned yesterday and when I arrived at the Justicars section I went to the wiki to brush up on the info about former Justicars. And there is precious little about that and a lot of that information is also contradictory like how Children of the Night says that Dmitra Illyanova, sire of Carlak was Bruhaj Justicar from 1920 to 1972 yet in Theo Bell's write up it is said that his sire, Don Cerro, was appointed Justicar in the 50s&quot;. It's annoying but also funny because usually different books contradict each other but this time it's contradicting information in the same book. What fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> And I agree, it gives space for creativity but I appreciate official info. Yes, I can always create my own NPCs and I do (one of my favourite NPCs was my Ventrue Justicar Lucius who was fucking up shit for my PCs) but I am a lore junkie so I love when there are some written characters that I could use or ignore. That's why I love books like Children of the Night because they give some interesting power players like Frederico di Padua, Samedi enforcer to the Camarilla. <br /> <br /> That's why I appreciate courts of the Damned because it has write ups for Camarilla's big honchos as well as important personas for the Anarch movement. And the drawn illustrations do not hurt either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T05:38:25-07:00","id":1561928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561882#post1561882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh right, I even forgot she was Lasombra in the Chaos Factor. I just remember us running the Sabbat (yes, I am a fan of clan Toreador). Her posing as Lasombra makes sense even if it is a retcon (I don't think it is ever explicitly mentioned in the books), vampires pretending to be other clans is nothing unheard of.<br /> <br /> And I know what you are saying about the regents. I was reading through Courts of the Damned yesterday and when I arrived at the Justicars section I went to the wiki to brush up on the info about former Justicars. And there is precious little about that and a lot of that information is also contradictory like how Children of the Night says that Dmitra Illyanova, sire of Carlak was Bruhaj Justicar from 1920 to 1972 yet in Theo Bell's write up it is said that his sire, Don Cerro, was appointed Justicar in the 50s&quot;. It's annoying but also funny because usually different books contradict each other but this time it's contradicting information in the same book. What fun <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I agree, it gives space for creativity but I appreciate official info. Yes, I can always create my own NPCs and I do (one of my favourite NPCs was my Ventrue Justicar Lucius who was fucking up shit for my PCs) but I am a lore junkie so I love when there are some written characters that I could use or ignore. That's why I love books like Children of the Night because they give some interesting power players like Frederico di Padua, Samedi enforcer to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> That's why I appreciate courts of the Damned because it has write ups for Camarilla's big honchos as well as important personas for the Anarch movement. And the drawn illustrations do not hurt either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've yet to get Courts of the Damned. V5 books have been slow to arrive here in the UK, so I've been waiting for several of them to become available first. I'm looking forward to it, though. However, I've intentionally ignored V5 continuity in my timeline, since it's basically an alternative history at this point. Where V20 generally tries to marry V2e and VRev contradictions, and only really ignores stuff from the very end of the line's run, V5 is a bit more cavalier with changing stuff up.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the &quot;she posed as Lasombra&quot; thing is just an assumption players have made, but it may have been in one of the novels (I haven't read all of those yet). However, V20 does have fake Galbraith send an invitation to Beckett using the Lasombra logo (BJD, p. 146). This implies that Sikorsky, at least, believed her to be Lasombra (or believed that she wanted to pose as Lasombra, so has done the same). I think that's maybe the first time it's officially been put into a sourcebook, and it's only really an oblique reference, but I'm happy to be corrected if anyone can find an earlier reference.<br /> <br /> Lucita at least confirms that others assumed her to be Lasombra on p. 148, when she says:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett's Jyhad Diary, p. 148</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Regent came over to the New World with your friend Helena, which would make her Toreador <i>antitribu</i> rather than a Keeper. Aristotle\u2019s merely written what most believe to be true.-L</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T18:57:49-07:00","id":1561951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561928#post1561928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've yet to get Courts of the Damned. V5 books have been slow to arrive here in the UK, so I've been waiting for several of them to become available first. I'm looking forward to it, though. However, I've intentionally ignored V5 continuity in my timeline, since it's basically an alternative history at this point. Where V20 generally tries to marry V2e and VRev contradictions, and only really ignores stuff from the very end of the line's run, V5 is a bit more cavalier with changing stuff up.<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the &quot;she posed as Lasombra&quot; thing is just an assumption players have made, but it may have been in one of the novels (I haven't read all of those yet). However, V20 does have fake Galbraith send an invitation to Beckett using the Lasombra logo (BJD, p. 146). This implies that Sikorsky, at least, believed her to be Lasombra (or believed that she wanted to pose as Lasombra, so has done the same). I think that's maybe the first time it's officially been put into a sourcebook, and it's only really an oblique reference, but I'm happy to be corrected if anyone can find an earlier reference.<br /> <br /> Lucita at least confirms that others assumed her to be Lasombra on p. 148, when she says:<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It must have been really hard for her to keep appearances since every time she showed up on a mirror, she either had to Dominate to forget about it or destroy the Cainite who realized the masquerade. Imagine the amount of blood feasts she assisted where blood pools lit by fire or light reflect those who drank from them. She did have Dominate at her sire's level though.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T19:26:11-07:00","id":1561952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561951#post1561951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It must have been really hard for her to keep appearances since every time she showed up on a mirror, she either had to Dominate to forget about it or destroy the Cainite who realized the masquerade. Imagine the amount of blood feasts she assisted where blood pools lit by fire or light reflect those who drank from them. She did have Dominate at her sire's level though.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>That's where &quot;pose&quot; differs from &quot;others assumed&quot;. Just look at how many people can believe in things that are demonstrably false with an easy search.<br /> <br /> If she never made any statement or effort, people would assume Lasombra because it's the most likely, most witnesses to get reflection would not comment on the fact, and even if one did, it wouldn't reach most others.<br /> <br /> She actually could publicly declare she's a Toreador and there would be still people saying she's Lasombra. Even some witnesses could conclude she found a way around the curse or some trick and never realize she maybe isn't a Lasombra at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-19T21:50:37-07:00","id":1561956,"title":"","content":"Even when you show some people proof that they are mistaken and they will double down on there notions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T11:10:30-07:00","id":1561974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561952#post1561952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's where &quot;pose&quot; differs from &quot;others assumed&quot;. Just look at how many people can believe in things that are demonstrably false with an easy search.<br /> <br /> If she never made any statement or effort, people would assume Lasombra because it's the most likely, most witnesses to get reflection would not comment on the fact, and even if one did, it wouldn't reach most others.<br /> <br /> She actually could publicly declare she's a Toreador and there would be still people saying she's Lasombra. Even some witnesses could conclude she found a way around the curse or some trick and never realize she maybe isn't a Lasombra at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this. The books don't say she personally posed as Lasombra; it's just a fan assumption. And as I say, New York City by Night repeatedly says that Sabbat vampires assume whoever's in charge is Lasombra because that's the way things usually are.<br /> <br /> Besides, there are Lasombra who have posed as Ventrue for centuries, so we know there are means to fake having a reflection (and presumably means to do the opposite). In Galbraith's case, there are also infernal investments that could do the trick.<br /> <br /> It's not that astonishing to think a Fifth Generation infernalist could pull this off she wanted to. But again, there's no evidence to suggest she wanted to or did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T15:00:58-07:00","id":1561979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561974#post1561974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly this. The books don't say she personally posed as Lasombra; it's just a fan assumption. And as I say, New York City by Night repeatedly says that Sabbat vampires assume whoever's in charge is Lasombra because that's the way things usually are.<br /> <br /> Besides, there are Lasombra who have posed as Ventrue for centuries, so we know there are means to fake having a reflection (and presumably means to do the opposite). In Galbraith's case, there are also infernal investments that could do the trick.<br /> <br /> It's not that astonishing to think a Fifth Generation infernalist could pull this off she wanted to. But again, there's no evidence to suggest she wanted to or did.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC it was on Masquerade of the Red Death (yeah, I know that it was considered not canon but that was probably around '98) or some other book in which it is stated that she was &quot;supposedly&quot; Lasombra, but I'm sure it is out there somewhere. We do know that she was 5th generation Toreador since Chaos Factor came out in '93, two years after VtM was released its 1st ed.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-20T17:18:03-07:00","id":1561980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561974#post1561974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, there are Lasombra who have posed as Ventrue for centuries, so we know there are means to fake having a reflection (and presumably means to do the opposite). In Galbraith's case, there are also infernal investments that could do the trick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although my personal canon is that he also never posed as Ventrue, because seriously, there's no crime in being a Lasombra Prince, it was kinda unnecessary as a setting element.<br /> <br /> But in the end, the mere fact she's powerful enough to fake being Toreador could make people assume she's doing that for no other reason than thinking it makes more sense.<br /> <br /> In the end, by Occam's Razor I think it would be to contrived to even say this is ambiguous, we have zero evidence that she tried to pass for Lasombra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T01:06:59-07:00","id":1561988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561979#post1561979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC it was on Masquerade of the Red Death (yeah, I know that it was considered not canon but that was probably around '98) or some other book in which it is stated that she was &quot;supposedly&quot; Lasombra, but I'm sure it is out there somewhere. We do know that she was 5th generation Toreador since Chaos Factor came out in '93, two years after VtM was released its 1st ed.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds about right. Interestingly, those books also have Galbraith &quot;disappear&quot;, assumed dead, only to return and start killing everyone. From what I remember, they contradict whole swathes of the lore, but they're good pulpy fun. Case in point: when Galbraith is told she can't just behead an archbishop, she basically screams, &quot;I'm Melinda fucking Galbraith!&quot; Her scenery chewing villainy is quite fun, IIRC, but I do prefer the more capable side of her we see in other books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T08:21:17-07:00","id":1561990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561980#post1561980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although my personal canon is that he also never posed as Ventrue, because seriously, there's no crime in being a Lasombra Prince, it was kinda unnecessary as a setting element.<br /> <br /> But in the end, the mere fact she's powerful enough to fake being Toreador could make people assume she's doing that for no other reason than thinking it makes more sense.<br /> <br /> In the end, by Occam's Razor I think it would be to contrived to even say this is ambiguous, we have zero evidence that she tried to pass for Lasombra.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I totally disagree with. No one says it's a crime to be a Lasombra prince in Camarilla but saying that a Ventrue prince and Lasombra prince are being treated the same way would be wrong. There is definitely more scrutiny on a Keeper in the Camarilla than on the King/Queen. <br /> <br /> I am not saying that Vitel had to pretend to be a Ventrue or even that it wasn't just a &quot;wow&quot; moment from the writers/developers in the Revised era. I am not against someone deciding they don't want this part of his story. It is not a mandatory fact that Vitel story needs to make sense, still it makes sense as part of his story. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-21T09:29:23-07:00","id":1561995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561990#post1561990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">saying that a Ventrue prince and Lasombra prince are being treated the same way would be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that.<br /> <br /> Didn't said it doesn't make sense, either.<br /> <br /> All I said is my headcanon. And I for one think an open Lasombra Prince would be interesting precisely because it's not the same. And I don't just remove this, I change his story.<br /> <br /> You're not welcome to disagree. I'm open to discuss ideas, official canon, etc. I'm not open to any random in the internet telling me if my HEADcanon is correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-24T23:04:28-07:00","id":1562138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561614#post1561614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Al-Ashrad's sire is Ur-Shulgi, which could imply that neither of them are Assamites. Interestingly, Izhim ur-Baal.apparently came out of Namtaru's hand with bleached hair and pale skin, despite being blackened with age before. Which... Yeah. There's clearly a link between pale-skinned &quot;Assamites&quot; and Baali influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say the revised Assamite clanbook (which mentioned al-Ashrad's skin condition being unique to him, so Izhim getting bleached wasn't known by that author/postdates that book/doesn't count since he started off darkening normally, whichever) also mentions at least one of al-Ashrad's childer, the sorcerer Amaravati, whose skin goes without comment in that book. He also has a VTES card that doesn't show him being pale at all either. I want to say another line in the clanbook mentions about two-thirds of the surviving Sorcerers in the modern age trace their lineage back to ur-Shulgi, and none of them get tagged as unusually light-skinned.<br /> <br /> So I'm assuming that <i>whatever</i> weirdness ur-Shulgi and al-Ashrad have going on, they at least count as Assamites enough to pass on that distinction to later generations. Al-Ashrad doesn't even need any of his sire's potential Baali shenanigans to be weird; he was a mortal mage and demon hunter who worked with Haqim's children for centuries before circumstances led to his Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2218-ideon","name":"Ideon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T05:44:06-07:00","id":1562223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1561995#post1561995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't say that.<br /> <br /> Didn't said it doesn't make sense, either.<br /> <br /> All I said is my headcanon. And I for one think an open Lasombra Prince would be interesting precisely because it's not the same. And I don't just remove this, I change his story.<br /> <br /> You're not welcome to disagree. I'm open to discuss ideas, official canon, etc. I'm not open to any random in the internet telling me if my HEADcanon is correct.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I am tired of this shit.<br /> <br /> You said it was &quot;uneccessary as a setting element&quot;. I am not disagreeing with your headcannon I am disagreeing with your assesment of the canon. So please stop responding to arguments I never made. <br /> <br /> There is a Lasombra prince in Giangaleazzo who made big show of joining Cam. That was not what Vitel wanted (or more precisely what the writers wanted).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T09:57:55-07:00","id":1562228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554876-timeline-of-vampire-the-masquerade?p=1562223#post1562223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You said it was &quot;uneccessary as a setting element&quot;. I am not disagreeing with your headcannon I am disagreeing with your assesment of the canon. So please stop responding to arguments I never made.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't made any argument in the sense that it was necessary. You argued it made sense. Those are not the same thing. I am not responding to arguments you never made, I'm trying to make sense of what you're disagreeing with.<br /> <br /> Do you think it was a necessary setting element? How so? Why the setting needs to have a Prince that's secretly a Lasombra?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-27T11:45:25-07:00","id":1562232,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that says that a Lasombra member of the Camarilla sect can't be Prince and be open about what clan they are apart of. Unless they just from time to time like to mess with the Ventrue for laughs or learning more of their rivals strengths and weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}